-- coa5-service-contracts.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 5 (directors' service contracts, ss 227 to 230) and Chapter 6 (contracts with sole
-- members who are directors, s 231): lines 3028-3072 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).
-- OFFENCES. "An offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default": whether an officer is in default is s 1121's answer (coa24),
-- an input here, `s 1121 the officer is in default`. The pounds that "level 3" or "level 5" on the standard scale stands for are not in the Act: inputs.
-- A DUTY is encoded twice where the text names a party and a time: as a decision function ("has the duty been met") and, where it can be run,
-- as a regulative rule with the same facts. A trace is read, not asserted, on the stable binary (NOTES.md).

§ `Chapter 5: directors' service contracts (ss 227 to 230)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 227 Directors' service contracts
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 227(1) arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `s 227(1)(a) a director of the company undertakes personally to perform services (as director or otherwise) for the company, or for a subsidiary of the company`
    `s 227(1)(b) services that a director of the company undertakes personally to perform are made available by a third party to the company, or to a subsidiary of the company`
    `s 227(1) some other arrangement`

-- src:3030 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a director's “service contract”, in relation to a company, means a contract under which—
-- src:3031 | (a) a director of the company undertakes personally to perform services (as director or otherwise) for the company, or for a subsidiary of the company, or
-- src:3032 | (b) services (as director or otherwise) that a director of the company undertakes personally to perform are made available by a third party to the company, or to a subsidiary of the company.
@ref s 227(1) a director's service contract (src:3030-3032)
GIVEN arrangement IS A `s 227(1) arrangement`
      `the arrangement is a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(1) the contract is a director's service contract` MEANS
    IF `the arrangement is a contract` AND (NOT (arrangement EQUALS `s 227(1) some other arrangement`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director's “service contract”, in relation to a company, means a contract under which— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:3033 | (2) The provisions of this Part relating to directors' service contracts apply to the terms of a person's appointment as a director of a company.
@ref s 227(2) appointment terms (src:3033-3033)
GIVEN `the terms are the terms of a person's appointment as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(2) the provisions of this Part relating to directors' service contracts apply to the terms` MEANS
    IF `the terms are the terms of a person's appointment as a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the terms of a person's appointment as a director of a company"

-- src:3034 | They are not restricted to contracts for the performance of services outside the scope of the ordinary duties of a director.
@ref s 227(2) not restricted (src:3034-3034)
`s 227(2) the provisions relating to directors' service contracts are restricted to contracts for services outside the scope of the ordinary duties of a director` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "They are not restricted to contracts for the performance of services outside the scope of the ordinary duties of a director"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 228 Copy of contract or memorandum of terms to be available for inspection
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- "the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for" is not in the Act: an input.
-- src:3048 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 228(6) the penalty (src:3048-3048)
`s 228(6) the penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:3048 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 228(6) the largest fine in pounds (src:3048-3048)
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 228(6) the largest fine in pounds` MEANS `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`

-- src:3048 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 228(6) the largest daily default fine in pounds (src:3048-3048)
GIVEN `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 228(6) the largest daily default fine in pounds` MEANS `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` TIMES 0.1

-- src:3036 | (1) A company must keep available for inspection—
-- src:3037 | (a) a copy of every director's service contract with the company or with a subsidiary of the company, or
-- src:3038 | (b) if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out the terms of the contract.
@ref s 228(1) keep a copy or memorandum available for inspection (src:3036-3038)
GIVEN `the contract is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the contract is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written memorandum setting out the terms is kept available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(1) the company has kept the copy or memorandum available for inspection` MEANS
    IF (`the contract is in writing` AND `a copy of the contract is kept available for inspection`)
       OR ((NOT `the contract is in writing`) AND `a written memorandum setting out the terms is kept available for inspection`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must keep available for inspection— (a) a copy of every director's service contract ..., or (b) if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out the terms of the contract" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

DECLARE `s 228(2) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 228(2)(a) the company's registered office`
    `s 228(2)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
    `s 228(2) some other place`

-- src:3039 | (2) All the copies and memoranda must be kept available for inspection at—
-- src:3040 | (a) the company's registered office, or
-- src:3041 | (b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 228(2) the place (src:3039-3041)
GIVEN place IS A `s 228(2) place`
      `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(2) the copies and memoranda are kept at a permitted place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 228(2)(a) the company's registered office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 228(2)(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN
         CONSIDER `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available for inspection at— (a) the company's registered office, or (b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which places the regulations under s 1136 specify is not in the sources
    WHEN `s 228(2) some other place` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available for inspection at— (a) the company's registered office, or (b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136"

-- "at least one year from the date of termination or expiry": the day a year on is counted in (fork F-228-1).
-- src:3042 | (3) The copies and memoranda must be retained by the company for at least one year from the date of termination or expiry of the contract and must be kept available for inspection during that time.
@ref s 228(3) retention (src:3042-3042)
GIVEN `the date of termination or expiry of the contract` IS A DATE
      `the date in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(3) the copies and memoranda must still be retained and kept available on the date` MEANS
    IF `the date in question` AT MOST `add years` `the date of termination or expiry of the contract` 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be retained by the company for at least one year from the date of termination or expiry of the contract and must be kept available for inspection during that time" (the period the text fixes has ended)

-- src:3043 | (4) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:3044 | (a) of the place at which the copies and memoranda are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:3045 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:3046 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 228(4) notice to the registrar (src:3043-3046)
GIVEN `the copies and memoranda have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(4) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in it` MEANS
    IF `the copies and memoranda have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE -- "The company must give notice to the registrar— (a) of the place at which the copies and memoranda are kept available for inspection, and (b) of any change in that place"

-- The same duty as a rule. The text of (4) states no time; the 14 days appear in (5) ("default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (4)"),
-- from which the offence arises, and that is the time used (counted from the day the duty arose).
DECLARE `s 228 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 228(4) give notice to the registrar of the place`

-- src:3043 | (4) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:3044 | (a) of the place at which the copies and memoranda are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:3045 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:3046 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
-- src:3047 | (5) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3), or default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (4), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 228(4) and (5) the duty to give notice, and the 14 days (src:3043-3047)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 228 action`
`s 228(4) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 228(4) give notice to the registrar of the place`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Officer in default` BECAUSE "s 228(5): default for 14 days in giving notice to the registrar is an offence by every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:3047 | (5) If default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3), or default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (4), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 228(5) the offence (src:3047-3047)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228(5) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3)` OR `the number of days default has been made in complying with subsection (4)` AT LEAST 14)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1), (2) or (3), or default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (4), an offence is committed"
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:3049 | (7) The provisions of this section apply to a variation of a director's service contract as they apply to the original contract.
@ref s 228(7) variation (src:3049-3049)
GIVEN `the change is a variation of a director's service contract` IS A BOOLEAN
