-- src:3051 | (1) Every copy or memorandum required to be kept under section 228 must be open to inspection by any member of the company without charge.
@ref s 229(1) inspection (src:3051-3051)
GIVEN `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept under section 228` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229(1) the person may inspect the copy or memorandum without charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the copy or memorandum is one required to be kept under section 228`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every copy or memorandum required to be kept under section 228"
        IF `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "open to inspection by any member of the company" (the subsection speaks of members)

-- src:3052 | (2) Any member of the company is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any such copy or memorandum.
@ref s 229(2) copy on request (src:3052-3052)
GIVEN `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the member has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229(2) the member is entitled to be provided with a copy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member is s 112's answer
        IF NOT (`s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any member of the company is entitled"
        IF `the member has made a request` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy" (not entitled until the request is made and the fee paid)

-- "within seven days after the request is received by the company": the copy is provided on or before the date the request was received plus seven days.
-- src:3053 | The copy must be provided within seven days after the request is received by the company.
@ref s 229(2) seven days (src:3053-3053)
GIVEN `the date the request is received by the company` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy is provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229(2) the copy has been provided in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the copy is provided` AT MOST `the date the request is received by the company` PLUS 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy must be provided within seven days after the request is received by the company"

DECLARE `s 229 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 229(2) provide the member with a copy`

-- src:3052 | (2) Any member of the company is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any such copy or memorandum.
-- src:3053 | The copy must be provided within seven days after the request is received by the company.
@ref s 229(2) the duty to provide the copy within seven days (src:3052-3053)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 229 action`
`s 229(2) the company's duty to provide the copy` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 229(2) provide the member with a copy`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 229(2): the copy was not provided within seven days after the request was received (an offence by every officer of the company who is in default, s 229(3))"

-- src:3054 | (3) If an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 229(3) the offence (src:3054-3054)
