        IF NOT (`an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused` OR `default is made in complying with subsection (2)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an inspection required under subsection (1) is refused, or default is made in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed"
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:3055 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 229(4) the penalty (src:3055-3055)
