§ `Chapter 6: contracts with sole members who are directors (s 231)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 231 Contract with sole member who is also a director
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- "(b) the sole member is also a director": by (5) a shadow director is treated as a director: the caller passes `s 231(5)`'s answer in that fact.
-- src:3061 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:3062 | (a) a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member,
-- src:3063 | (b) the sole member is also a director of the company, and
-- src:3064 | (c) the contract is not entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business.
@ref s 231(1) application (src:3061-3064)
GIVEN `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sole member is also a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member` AND `the sole member is also a director of the company` AND (NOT `the contract is entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a limited company having only one member enters into a contract with the sole member, (b) the sole member is also a director of the company, and (c) the contract is not entered into in the ordinary course of the company's business"

-- src:3070 | (5) For the purposes of this section a shadow director is treated as a director.
@ref s 231(5) shadow director (src:3070-3070)
GIVEN `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(5) the shadow director is treated as a director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a shadow director is treated as a director"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is s 251's answer

