GIVEN `s 231(2) the company must ensure the terms are set out or recorded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) the company has complied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 231(2) the company must ensure the terms are set out or recorded`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the duty arises is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company must, unless the contract is in writing" (no duty arises)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the terms are set out in a written memorandum` OR `the terms are recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors following the making of the contract`
         THEN JUST TRUE
