DECLARE `s 231 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 231(2) set the terms out in a written memorandum or record them in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the contract`

-- The duty as a rule. The text states no time: "the first meeting of the directors of the company following the making of the contract" fixes the
-- meeting, not a number of days, so no WITHIN is written and none is invented.
-- src:3065 | (2) The company must, unless the contract is in writing, ensure that the terms of the contract are either—
-- src:3066 | (a) set out in a written memorandum, or
-- src:3067 | (b) recorded in the minutes of the first meeting of the directors of the company following the making of the contract.
@ref s 231(2) the duty (src:3065-3067)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 231 action`
`s 231(2) the company's duty to ensure the terms are set out or recorded` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 231(2) set the terms out in a written memorandum or record them in the minutes of the first directors' meeting following the contract`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 231(2): the terms of a contract with the sole member who is a director were neither set out in a written memorandum nor recorded in the minutes"

-- src:3068 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 231(3) the offence (src:3068-3068)
GIVEN `s 231(2) the company has complied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(3) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 231(2) the company has complied` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the company failed to comply is not known
        IF `s 231(2) the company has complied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section an offence is committed" (the company complied)
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:3069 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 231(4) the penalty (src:3069-3069)
`s 231(4) the penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:3069 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 231(4) the largest fine in pounds (src:3069-3069)
GIVEN `the pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 231(4) the largest fine in pounds` MEANS `the pounds that level 5 on the standard scale stands for`

-- src:3071 | (6) Failure to comply with this section in relation to a contract does not affect the validity of the contract.
@ref s 231(6) validity of the contract (src:3071-3071)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with this section in relation to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
